"""Northern Barrens hub: the outer direction the old accept line used to give."""

STORY = {
    'nb_peat_hearts': ("Deep in the fens, the peat has started to move. I'd like some credit for how calmly I said that, because it took me a season to manage it.\n\nThe Peat Shamblers are mud, root, and old bog-oak that's been down there since before the Horde crossed the sea, and they shuffle up and down the causeway at night. They don't hunt, but anything on the causeway while they're at it simply gets in the way. At the heart of each one there's a core, and it's warm the way a banked fire is, hours after, and it doesn't go out when you take it out of the thing.\n\nI can burn those through a whole cold winter, and my wardens can stop choosing between firewood and sleep. You'll have to break them for it. Hit the middle. The Slug Fens are south of here.", None),
    'nb_old_mire_maw': ("There's something at the bottom of the deep fen, and I've spent three years not asking anyone about it. Old Mire-Maw is a crocolisk older than the causeway and wider than a wagon, and my grandfather's people laid that causeway.\n\nI've lost three wardens to it. I knew all three, and I sent all three. The first was an accident, the second was bad luck, and the third was me still calling it bad luck. That's all of my reasoning, and I won't make it sound more strategic than it is.\n\nIt hides in the deep pools at the end of the causeway, with Fenwater Crocolisks round it. Don't stand in the water, and don't stand near the water. The Slug Fens are south of here.", None),
    'nb_rig_crews': ("I'm Nix, and I call myself a sludge inspector, which is a title I made up for a job nobody's hiring for.\n\nI worked for the Venture Company for years, and they were good years, honestly. Then I found out what they were doing down in the fen. Now I sit in a rusted shack out there counting crews, and come in to Far Watch to report it. They're drilling day and night, the ground is bleeding black and it's reaching the water, and I've watched the edge of the stain move for eleven months.\n\nI want the Venture Co. Oil Drillers gone. I know most of them, and I trained some of them, and I'm asking anyway. The drillers are the loud ones. Stop the noise, and the guards come out, and the guards are quieter and nastier. The Sludge Fen is north of here.", None),
    'nb_pressure_gauges': ("Every rig has a gauge, and every gauge tells you how hard they're drilling, how deep, and how close this whole fen is to going up. Nix used to read them for Venture, and so did I, before we both walked out. The last number is the one we need, and you can't get it with a glass from a hill.\n\nThe Pumpjack Guards keep the gauges on a chain at the belt. Cut the chain, and don't fight the guard's friends if you can help it. They fight as a unit, and a chain is a moment's work if nobody's shouting yet. The rig's in the Sludge Fen, north of here.", None),
    'nb_sludge_samples': ("Where the oil's pooled, the sludge has started to move. The Sludge Elementals are black, sticky and very angry, and I don't think that last word's a figure of speech. Something down there got poured into enough of itself to start having opinions.\n\nI want samples, not for the fen, which is past arguing with, but for the Company. The Board will say the drilling's clean right up until somebody puts a jar on the table. I've sat in those rooms and watched exactly that happen over something smaller.\n\nTake the samples from the middle of them, where it's purest, which is also where they are. They leave a slick behind them, so watch your footing. The goop doesn't come off, ever. I've still got some. The Sludge Fen is north of here.", None),
    'nb_claim_jumpers': ("I'm Gruda, the claim surveyor, and before you ask, yes, I've got the paperwork.\n\nThe Boulder Lode was a Horde claim, filed, stamped and witnessed by two people who are still alive and will still say so. Then the Venture Company moved in, and now their miners swing picks on my walls. The paperwork isn't helping. I read the relevant line aloud at the mine mouth to a goblin with a clipboard. He wrote something down and nothing happened, and I'm fairly sure what he wrote was my name.\n\nSo the paperwork stays in my pack now. Go in and clear the Venture Co. Miners out of the lower galleries. They aren't soldiers, and I'd like that said, but they'll hit you with a pick all the same. The Boulder Lode Mine is north of here.", None),
    'nb_prospector_delvik': ("Delvik was my partner for twenty-two years. We filed the Boulder Lode together, with both our names on the stamp, and his hand is on half of the original survey.\n\nHe sold the claim's map to the Venture Company for a promise and a bag of silver, and I've had a long time to decide which half of that insults me more. Now he's in a side adit with a rifle and a bad conscience, and he hasn't come out, and the Company hasn't come to get him either. That's what the promise was worth.\n\nHe's in the side adit off the middle gallery, behind the rubble pile. He shoots first. The Venture Co. Tinkerers keep him company, and once they're cleared, you've done most of the work. The Boulder Lode Mine is north of here.", None),
    'nb_foreman_grills': ("At the top of the mine, round a vein of blue crystal, Foreman Grills runs the Company's crew. He wears an iron hat and carries a bullhorn, and in his own estimation he's the cleverest man ever to hold a pick.\n\nHe's the loudest man ever to hold a pick, I'll grant him that. But he's been working that blue seam for four months and taking it out in the wrong order, and anybody who'd actually read a vein would know it, and nobody up there will tell him. That's how the whole claim gets ruined even if we win.\n\nHe's in the crystal chamber at the top, and the Venture Co. Overseers hold the way up. Kill them, and he's alone, if you can call a man with a bullhorn alone. The Boulder Lode Mine is north of here.", None),
}
